      "expr": "[t]='a'",
      "values": {
        "t": "A"
      },
      "expect": false,
      "expectCi": true
    },
    {
      "_comment": "Case folding. expect is the exact comparison every gate uses (and an @UVASSERT with \"caseSensitive\": true); expectCi is the @UVASSERT default, which folds ASCII A-Z to a-z on both sides before comparing. Only those 26 letters fold, identically in both runtimes, so accented letters keep their case."
    },
    {
      "name": "ci_eq_literal",
